WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.030
Mobile Task Forces.

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:06.620
They’re the elite special forces units of
the SCP Foundation.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:11.250
Whenever a particularly dangerous anomaly
rears its ugly head, you can guarantee that

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.270
these members of personnel with highly specialized
skillsets will be sent in to take care of

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.270
business.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:22.260
A lot of the time, MTFs are relocated between
different Foundation facilities, or sent from

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:26.440
location to location, hence the “Mobile”
part of the name.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:32.090
They vary in size and function too, with some
teams being small, covert investigators and

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.980
intelligence gatherers.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:39.070
Meanwhile, others might be huge battalions
consisting of hundreds of troops, vehicles,

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:42.810
and enough heavy-duty firepower to put The
Terminator to shame.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:47.440
Whether it’s containing a newly-emerged
SCP, or helping the Foundation to get a flighty

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.150
anomaly back into its cage and keeping it
there, the MTFs are who you’re gonna call

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.280
when it all hits the fan.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:01:00.860
They’re the best of the SCP Foundation’s
best, and few represent that better than MTF

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.860
Tau-5.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.860
If you’re at all familiar with the SCP Foundation,
then there’s a good chance you’ve heard

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:11.970
of the iconic Mobile Task Force Tau-5, also
known by their collective codename “Samsara.”

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:16.170
Take everything you know about an average
task force, give them leagues better equipment

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.960
and training, and put them on anomalous super-steroids,
and you’re still likely to get an MTF who

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.049
can only dream of getting on Samsara’s level.

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.920
In our series on the infamous Site-13, you’ve
seen these badasses take on horrors beyond

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.240
description and not even blink, even rescuing
other Mobile Task Forces from the jaws of

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.690
death on many occasions.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:41.930
Why are they given such prestige, even in
a crowded field of elite Foundation operatives?

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:47.600
It’s because the four members of the Samsara
team are unlike any other MTFs on a fundamental

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:53.549
level, given that each one of them was created
from the flesh of a dead god.

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:55.210
Sounds cool enough on its own, right?

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:59.840
Well, not only are Tau-5 specially created
from a divine deity, but each of them has

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.970
also had their bodies enhanced with cutting-edge
cybernetics.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:10.009
These immortal cyborgs can be upgraded at
any time, as and when the need arises, using

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:14.769
the latest of the Foundation’s experimental
weaponry to combat and contain all kinds of

00:02:14.769 --> 00:02:19.739
anomalous threats from the thaumaturgic and
psionic, to even powerful, reality-warping

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:23.160
entities that a normal MTF couldn’t dream
of handling.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:30.239
Together, Samsara consists of two male operatives,
named Irantu and Munru, and two females, Nanku

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:31.239
and Onru.

00:02:31.239 --> 00:02:35.569
And that’s all you need to know before we
delve into the insanity that comes next.

00:02:35.569 --> 00:02:40.550
Buckle up and put on your SCRAMBLE goggles,
it’s time for Avatara.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:45.879
Long ago, there was a deity known as the Lord
of Endowments, a god who once assumed the

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:50.090
persona of Prometheus - No, not the Ridley
Scott movie.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:54.749
Prometheus was a figure from Ancient Greek
mythology, who stole the gift of knowledge

00:02:54.749 --> 00:02:59.829
from the gods of Mount Olympus and gifted
it to the people of Earth, often represented

00:02:59.829 --> 00:03:01.810
as metaphorical fire.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:06.159
As punishment for his transgression, Prometheus
was chained to the side of a mountain, where

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:10.680
every day he would have his liver pecked out
by birds, only for it to grow back overnight

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.939
so the birds could feed on him again the next
day.

00:03:13.939 --> 00:03:18.749
So, our Lord of Endowment – stop giggling,
you at the back – gave himself a body of

00:03:18.749 --> 00:03:22.999
flesh so that he might walk upon the Earth
as a giant humanoid.

00:03:22.999 --> 00:03:28.089
His goal was to, like Prometheus, provide
mankind with knowledge and power, to grant

00:03:28.089 --> 00:03:31.859
them technology, and then redefine what it
meant to be human.

00:03:31.859 --> 00:03:36.409
The Lord amassed followers as a result, and
began to conquer new territories to expand

00:03:36.409 --> 00:03:37.409
his power.

00:03:37.409 --> 00:03:42.260
However, something changed and the Lord gradually
began to die.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.250
Whether it was the result of him becoming
flesh and therefore mortal - a betrayal by

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:51.329
his armies of followers - or punishment from
the other Gods for his exploits, the Lord

00:03:51.329 --> 00:03:57.079
of Endowment decided to split his mortal form
into three parts in order to survive.

00:03:57.079 --> 00:04:02.340
These were his Mind, Body and Spirit, and
they were hidden across the Earth, with his

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:07.959
Body being buried deep within the Tabernas
Desert in Spain, where his Mind also slept

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:09.180
within his body.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.129
Jump forward several thousands of years and
a group known as Prometheus Labs discovered

00:04:13.129 --> 00:04:15.659
the dormant flesh body of the Lord of Endowment.

00:04:15.659 --> 00:04:20.720
Prometheus Labs was once a Group of Interest
to the SCP Foundation, known for researching

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.660
anomalous objects with the goal of using them
to develop new technological breakthroughs.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:30.170
Unearthing the Lord’s Body, the Prometheus
scientists discovered that the body’s liver

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:33.030
contained cells that could endlessly regenerate.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:38.730
Eventually, harvesting and researching these
cells resulted in a brand new research project.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:42.510
The goal: to create a group of immortal warriors.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:47.650
Prometheus Labs took four volunteers and uploaded
their consciousnesses to a computer, hoping

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:52.560
to then download them into new bodies that
were cloned from the regenerating cells.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.600
The thought was, if one of these cloned bodies
was destroyed or somehow became so badly damaged

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.930
that it couldn’t be used, then this process
could be used to upload the same mind to a

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:06.810
fresh body, as simple as booting up a new
computer with an old harddrive.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.930
The project did produce some results, seeing
the creation of some mass-produced cyborg

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:13.790
warriors later known as SCP-1637.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:18.780
However, the research was cut short when a
surviving group of the Lord of Endowment’s

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.030
followers stormed Prometheus Labs.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:25.110
The followers raided the entire facility,
shooting the newly-cloned bodies that were

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:30.100
intended to be the hosts for the four consciousnesses
that had been saved to the computer.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:35.120
But even those were destroyed, along with
all the backup drives that contained copies

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.930
of the four minds.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.220
The Lord’s followers destroyed the Prometheus
facility, but the machine used to create the

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.450
clones miraculously survived.

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:48.630
It began gradually creating four new bodies,
despite sustaining heavy damage.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:54.660
The problem was, the minds and bodies of the
four volunteers were all gone, their lives,

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.270
thoughts, emotions, imagination, everything.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:02.270
Their humanity had been stored on a hard drive
that the followers had destroyed.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:08.600
But still, the machine did what machines do,
it cloned four new bodies.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:13.170
But there was nothing to inhabit them, nothing
more than a simple template: two genders,

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.640
and four names.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.130
Years go by, and Prometheus Labs suffered
another major accident which eventually led

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.950
to the organization disbanding.

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:26.840
However, some of their former scientists were
scooped up by the SCP Foundation, including

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.940
one doctor who had survived the attack at
the cloning facility.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.890
He took a group of the Foundation’s agents
to the location of that old project, where

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:40.690
they found four, almost featureless fleshy
shells, empty but ready to be transformed

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:45.530
into an asset the likes of which the Foundation
had never possessed before.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:51.090
The Prometheus Labs project that had almost
been for nothing lived on: Samsara.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:56.800
More time passes, until the members of MTF
Tau-5, also known as Samsara, were eventually

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.070
sent in to deal with a new anomaly that had
started to spread.

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:05.090
It originated from within a seemingly ordinary
farmhouse, however whenever anything organic

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.210
entered, it would rapidly become cancerous.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:12.690
In much the same vein, anything mechanical
brought into the house would break down.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:17.070
This meant that sending in any human personnel
or even unmanned drones were options that

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:22.600
were off the table for the Foundation, so
instead they called in Samsara.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:26.570
After all, if you need to send someone into
a house that causes certain death, why not

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:29.020
four functionally immortal cyborgs?

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:33.720
The members of Tau-5 were all constructed
from the same basic mind template, meaning

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.610
that all four of them lacked any real humanity.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:42.170
They react to anomalies very casually in terms
of their emotions, but respond extremely seriously

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:45.730
in terms of executing a task or containing
an SCP.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:50.210
Granted, this makes them a formidable fighting
force, but even though they try to hide it

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:55.690
behind acting human, Tau-5 have very little
understanding of emotions.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:59.680
As they entered the house, they heard the
sound of religious chanting and began to follow

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.410
it back to its source.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.940
In the bedroom, Samsara discovered a figure,
hidden behind a tumor so big that it appeared

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:09.400
to just be one huge mass of twisted flesh.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:14.560
“Provide him your flesh,” the creature
chanted, “Sate its thirst…

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.860
Give it your flesh that he may make you gods!”

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:21.970
Tau-5 were given the order to terminate the
creature that seemed to be the source of the

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:25.870
anomaly, but their shots only ricocheted off
the fleshy mass.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.870
The entity could not be killed by anything
not made from flesh.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:34.580
Irantu ordered Nanku to hand him her pistol,
and didn’t hesitate to shoot her multiple

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.371
times in the neck.

00:08:36.371 --> 00:08:40.809
He started hacking away at the dead Nanku’s
neck with a combat knife, while Onru and Munru

00:08:40.809 --> 00:08:43.579
helped Irantu finish decapitating her.

00:08:43.579 --> 00:08:47.699
Taking a grenade from Nanku’s belt, he stuffed
it into the mouth of his teammate’s severed

00:08:47.699 --> 00:08:51.920
head, pulled the pin, and threw it deep into
the cancerous mass.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:56.390
Diving out of harm’s way in the last second,
the remaining members of Samsara took cover

00:08:56.390 --> 00:09:01.180
as the grenade detonated, killing the anomaly
and showering the room with gooey bits of

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.870
muscles, intestines, brain tissue, and bone
marrow.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.399
Hope you weren’t eating while watching this
one, folks!

00:09:07.399 --> 00:09:12.279
They had no reservations about killing one
of their own, but Tau-5 had neutralized the

00:09:12.279 --> 00:09:16.089
anomaly, and its effect had stopped spreading
outside the farmhouse.

00:09:16.089 --> 00:09:21.649
Samsara re-entered the bedroom, only for one
of them, Munru, to discover something among

00:09:21.649 --> 00:09:24.550
the blood, guts, and viscera that remained.

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:30.009
Underneath piles of flesh, stained with meat
was a small, leather-bound book, Munru took

00:09:30.009 --> 00:09:32.209
it with him, hiding it away.

00:09:32.209 --> 00:09:36.050
This tome was a grimoire, a type of ancient
textbook of magic.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:41.240
Typically, a grimoire includes instructions
on how to create magical objects, talismans,

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:45.339
amulets and the like, or a number of spells
and magic charms.

00:09:45.339 --> 00:09:50.709
But some grimoires also instruct a reader
on how to summon or invoke supernatural entities,

00:09:50.709 --> 00:09:57.760
calling forth beings from the great beyond
like angels, spirits, demons, and deities.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:02.189
And this particular book described how to
summon the essence of a certain Promethean

00:10:02.189 --> 00:10:05.410
plunderer, the Lord of Endowment himself.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:10.529
Somehow, the cancerous, tumor-spreading entity
from the farmhouse, that affected both flesh

00:10:10.529 --> 00:10:14.449
and technology, seemed to have been created
by this book.

00:10:14.449 --> 00:10:18.279
So, why would one of MTF Tau-5 take the grimoire?

00:10:18.279 --> 00:10:22.629
Surely as a member of Samsara, Munru would
normally react to anomalies with the same

00:10:22.629 --> 00:10:27.509
emotionless pragmatism he and his teammates
shared, and would never think to stash this

00:10:27.509 --> 00:10:29.199
spellbook on his person?

00:10:29.199 --> 00:10:35.329
Unless, of course, Munru was being manipulated
by some outside force without realizing it.

00:10:35.329 --> 00:10:40.940
The Mind of the Lord, knowing that this book
was an important tool for his resurrection,

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:44.059
had managed to influence Munru into keeping
the grimoire.

00:10:44.059 --> 00:10:48.480
The members of Samsara returned to headquarters,
where they all began looking over the book

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.029
over the next two weeks.

00:10:50.029 --> 00:10:54.699
Nanku’s head was reformed and meticulously
put back together by the Foundation, left

00:10:54.699 --> 00:10:59.519
with only the scars from all the stitching
around her face, head and neck.

00:10:59.519 --> 00:11:05.019
Luckily for Irantu, the Tau-5s lacked the
emotional capacity to hold grudges; after

00:11:05.019 --> 00:11:09.389
all, think about it, how would you feel if
your co-worker decided to behead you and use

00:11:09.389 --> 00:11:14.660
your severed head as a bomb?

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:19.949
As the Tau-5 team studied the book, they found
themselves enjoying it, learning about a place

00:11:19.949 --> 00:11:22.750
where they could learn more about acting like
people.

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:28.689
A place they then hoped to visit, perhaps,
because it was the place they’d first started.

00:11:28.689 --> 00:11:32.880
If you were paying attention earlier in this
video, you’ll remember we told you the MTF

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.619
Tau-5 members were created from the flesh
of a dead god.

00:11:36.619 --> 00:11:41.930
And this particular dead god buried his body
in the Tabernas Desert in Spain.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:46.509
It was none other than the Lord of Endowment
that had been used to create the four immortal

00:11:46.509 --> 00:11:48.800
cyborgs of MTF Tau-5.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:55.629
The Samsara team had come from him, and now
he was trying to tempt them back...

00:11:55.629 --> 00:12:00.721
Now go check out “SCP Elite Mobile Task
Force Explained” and “SCP-1730 - What

00:12:00.721 --> 00:12:02.389
Happened to Site-13?

00:12:02.389 --> 00:12:06.800
The Full Story Compilation” for more of
Samsara and the other teams they work with!

